  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Two to four trucks per team on a real beach volleyball court; one-on-one
    is also supported. Drive and ACTION to suspension-jump. Your actual bumper/body
    contact determines the return: approach facing over the net, hit under the ball
    for a loft, time an aerial strike for a stronger spike. You cannot directly steer
    or teleport the ball. Three touches per team; a fourth or consecutive double
    touch loses the rally. Crossing the net resets the touch count. A ball touching
    your court gives the other team a point; the last touching team loses an out-of-bounds
    shot. The net and posts are physical. The winning team serves the next rally
    after a grounded countdown. Default15points, win by two, cap21;7/21options. AI
    predicts actual flight and assigns a primary receiver while teammates cover.
    Selected weather and wind affect the shared physical ball. Shared/chase/full-cab,
    free look, horn, Your Crew and optional AI cameras use standard collection controls.
    Results include contact/spike/save statistics and recorded highlights. Rematch
    restores all participants and score.'
